<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chaulukya dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">942 CE – 1244 CE (approx.) · capital Anahilavada</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Solanki dynasty of Gujarat, whose patronage produced the Modhera Sun temple, the Rani ki Vav stepwell and the marble temples of Mount Abu.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 942 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mularaja">Mularaja</a>, according to tradition the nephew of the last <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chavda-dynasty">Chavda dynasty</a> king, seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-gujarat">Anahilavada</a> and founded the dynasty. He and his successors expanded across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cutch-state">Kutch</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>, fighting the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chahamanas-of-shakambhari">Chahamanas of Shakambhari</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/paramara-dynasty">Paramara dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/western-chalukya-empire">Western Chalukya Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhima-i-chaulukya-dynasty">Bhima I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> sacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somnath-temple">Somnath temple</a> in 1025, but the kingdom recovered quickly: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modhera-sun-temple">Modhera Sun temple</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rani">Rani</a> ki Vav stepwell, built by Bhima's queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udayamati">Udayamati</a>, date from his reign, and his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vimal-shah">Vimala</a> built the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilwara-temples">Dilwara</a> temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-abu">Mount Abu</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayasimha-siddharaja">Jayasimha Siddharaja</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumarapala-chaulukya-dynasty">Kumarapala</a> ruled at the height of Chaulukya power; the Jain scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hemachandra">Hemachandra</a> served their courts, and Kumarapala became a patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jainism">Jainism</a>. Maritime trade made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> wealthy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mularaja-ii">Mularaja II</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> in 1178, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutb-ud-din-aibak">Qutb al-Din Aibak</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-gujarat">Anahilavada</a> in 1197. The dynasty weakened, and around 1244 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghel">Vaghela</a> branch took the throne.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chaulukya-dynasty.jpg" alt="Chaulukya dynasty" width="320" height="296"><figcaption>Image: Map created from DEMIS Mapserver, which are public domain. Koba-chan. Reference: [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Chaulukyas.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>942 CE – 1244 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Anahilavada</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mularaja, Jayasimha Siddharaja, Kumarapala</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Apabhramsha, Old Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Solanki dynasty, Chalukyas of Gujarat, Chaulukyas of Anahilavada</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1093&amp;focus=chaulukya-dynasty" aria-label="Chaulukya dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6786 1331 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chaulukya dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7106 1587h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7106 1587h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=1093&amp;focus=chaulukya-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
